# L §5.19 covered, L §4.5 (tally 2.1.8 R12; T's p9b): covered(x, span) is a hole only where a cover is undecided: st,
# known in a window that holds the cut, covers konto in March, so covered is HOLE-IMPRECISE naming st (c1), and
# windows each splits it true, then false (c2). 2.1.7's refcore printed false, never a hole.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-05-10
  start 2026-03-01
  end 2026-06-30

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input bank: observed
input amt: money PLN
input lvl: num

move pay[m in months]: transfers
  on start_of(m)
  leg cash from world to konto amount amt

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  amt = 10.00 PLN "s"
  lvl = 0 "s"
  opening[konto] = 0.00 PLN at 2026-03-01 start "s"

version st
  cite s
  governs 2026-03
  known window(2026-04-01, 2026-04-20)
  covers konto
  bank[r1] = (on: 2026-03-03, kind: transfers, leg cash from world to konto amount 7.00 PLN, fulfils: pay[2026-03]) "r"

ask c1: covered(konto, 2026-03) as known 2026-04-10
ask c2: covered(konto, 2026-03) as known 2026-04-10 windows each
=== expect
c1: ?"date within window(2026-04-01, 2026-04-20) not precise enough for the cut 2026-04-10" (st)
  cut 2026-04-10
c2 [known of st = 2026-04-01 .. 2026-04-10]: true
  cut 2026-04-10
c2 [known of st = 2026-04-11 .. 2026-04-20]: false
  cut 2026-04-10
warning: WARN-UNREAD input lvl is read by nothing
